---
// DRAFT: written from what the app does today (see travel-app/README.md and
// docs/plan.md). Have it reviewed before launch, then remove `noindex` and
// take "/privacy" out of sitemapExclude in astro.config.mjs.
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import { site } from "../site.config";

const metaDescription =
  "What Travel Map & Journal keeps about you, who can see it, the services it uses for maps, search and exchange rates, and how to download or delete it.";
---

<Layout title="Privacy" description={metaDescription} noindex>
  <article class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-4 pt-20 pb-28 sm:px-8 [&_h2]:mt-12 [&_h2]:mb-3 [&_h2]:text-3xl [&_h2]:font-semibold [&_h2]:text-ink [&_li]:mb-2 [&_p]:mb-4 [&_p]:text-body [&_ul]:mb-4 [&_ul]:list-disc [&_ul]:pl-6 [&_ul]:text-body">
    <h1 class="mb-4 text-5xl font-semibold text-ink">Privacy</h1>
    <p class="text-xl">{site.name} is a private travel journal. Here's what it keeps, who can see it, and how to take it with you.</p>

    <h2>What it keeps</h2>
    <ul>
      <li>Your account: your name, email, and a hashed password (or your Google login, if you sign in with Google).</li>
      <li>What you add: trips, spots, notes, ratings, homes, your wishlist, and the expenses and splits on your trips.</li>
      <li>One cover photo per trip or home, if you add one. Location data is removed from photos when they're uploaded.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Who can see it</h2>
    <p>Only you, unless you share. There's no public profile, feed or followers.</p>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Share links</strong> show a read-only page of one trip or destination to anyone who has the link. A spots-only link never shows costs or who went. Stopping sharing deletes the link.</li>
      <li><strong>People on a trip</strong> you've shared with them see that trip, and can add to it if you allow it.</li>
      <li>Your wishlist and your homes' dates are never on share links.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Services it uses</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><strong>Cloudflare</strong> hosts the app, its database and photos.</li>
      <li><strong>Photon</strong> (OpenStreetMap) answers place searches. What you type in a search is sent to it; your account isn't.</li>
      <li><strong>OpenFreeMap</strong> serves the map tiles.</li>
      <li><strong>Frankfurter</strong> (European Central Bank rates) supplies exchange rates. No personal data is sent.</li>
      <li><strong>Google</strong>, only if you choose to sign in with Google.</li>
    </ul>

    <h2>Your data is yours</h2>
    <p>
      “Download your data” in Settings gives you everything you've written in one file, any time. Deleting your account deletes your
      trips, spots and photos. Spots you added to someone else's trip pass to that trip's owner.
    </p>

    <h2>Questions</h2>
    <p>[Contact email to add before launch.]</p>
  </article>
</Layout>
